{
  "requirement": "Each bundled skill's workflow MUST end by naming the bundled skill for the next task, or, when different outcomes lead to different tasks, the skill for each such outcome. An outcome that leads to no further task needs no skill named. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:\n\n:::{sites} skills\n```yaml\nlanguage: markdown\npaths: [assets/skills]\nrule:\n  kind: minus_metadata\nmatch:\n  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"\nno_match:\n  - \"# Example\\n\"\n```\n:::",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** The text has one obligation: each bundled skill's workflow ends by naming the skill for the next task, or one skill per outcome. An outcome that leads to no further task needs no skill named. Every bundled skill is a site, and each site upholds this on its own, so the obligation needs no separate test here. I did not vet the sites.\n\n**Site query `skills`.** It uses `kind: minus_metadata` on markdown under `assets/skills`. I ran it and it returned five files:\n- `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md`\n- `assets/skills/habeas-refactor/SKILL.md`\n\nA search for `^name: ` found front matter in exactly these five skill files. The only other hits were CI workflow YAML files, which are outside the skills path. The `references/*.md` files carry no skill front matter, so the query correctly leaves them out. The query neither misses a skill nor selects anything outside the requirement's scope.\n\n**Query snippets.** The match snippet is a document with `name` front matter and a heading. The no_match snippet is the same document without front matter. Together they show the metadata condition, which is the only condition the query has.\n\n**Extra test.** `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skill_workflows_end_by_naming_the_skill_for_the_next_task]` also checks the last workflow step of all five skills for the expected next-skill names. It checks that the `habeas` routing table names every other skill. It is supplementary evidence and not the only check of the obligation.",
  "references": "cad77bef8fd9a6e827e81314c255639bcbcc74e3c865da250136997ac253fa61",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.cli.skill_conventions.next",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.cli.skill_conventions.next"
      ],
      "text": [
        "::::{req} skill_conventions.next",
        "Each bundled skill's workflow MUST end by naming the bundled skill for the next task, or, when different outcomes lead to different tasks, the skill for each such outcome. An outcome that leads to no further task needs no skill named. Each bundled skill, recognized by its front matter, is a site:",
        "",
        ":::{sites} skills",
        "```yaml",
        "language: markdown",
        "paths: [assets/skills]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: minus_metadata",
        "match:",
        "  - \"---\\nname: example\\n---\\n\\n# Example\\n\"",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"# Example\\n\"",
        "```",
        ":::",
        "::::"
      ]
    },
